3	 * (docs/gem5-fi/lsu/05-frequency-and-sampling.md r2-r8), EVENT-normalized:
4	 * the denominator is the injector's eligible-event stream, NOT CPU cycles
5	 * (the ooo track's chaos_trigger.hh stays cycle-based — different tracks,
6	 * different denominators, no mixing; W2 R1 ruling 2026-09-25).
7	 *
8	 * Tiers (05 r2-r8):
9	 *   F0 single transient — uniform over eligible events after warm-up;
10	 *   F1/F2/F3 — mean interval 1,000,000 / 100,000 / 10,000 eligible events,
11	 *              each next interval = U[iv/2, 3*iv/2) (±50% jitter, 05 r3-r5);
12	 *   F4 short burst — every 100,000 eligible events fire once, then pollute
13	 *              2-4 consecutive eligible events (05 r6);
14	 *   F5 permanent — from the first eligible event after warm-up to end of run
15	 *              (one bit/field per run; target choice is the injector's);
16	 *   F6 deterministic event — inject ONCE at the first occurrence of the
17	 *              specified event type (05 r7; event sources per 09 §2.1 map:
18	 *              TlbHit[FS-only]/SqForward/DirtyEviction/CasSuccess).
19	 *
20	 * Funnel counts (04 L0): attempted (hook invocations) / eligible (passed the
21	 * injector's eligibility filter) / injected (fault written). The ACTIVATED
22	 * count (fault consumed downstream) is the L0 read-back layer's verdict —
23	 * deliberately NOT counted here (W3 delivers it; W2 R2 ruling). End-of-run
24	 * summary line: CHAOS_LSU_TRIGGER: injector= tier= attempted= eligible=
25	 * injected=.
26	 *
27	 * F6 event notification: the single-consumer function pointer below is
28	 * single-core-SE scoped (one LSU consumer per run — the 337-cell grid runs
29	 * one injector per run by construction). A multicore/FS generalization is
30	 * W8's business, recorded here honestly.
31	 */
32	#ifndef __CPU_O3_CHAOS_LSU_TRIGGER_HH__
33	#define __CPU_O3_CHAOS_LSU_TRIGGER_HH__
34	
35	#include <cstdint>
36	#include <cstdio>
37	
38	#include "cpu/o3/chaos_event_sample.hh"
39	#include "sim/core.hh"         // curTick() [LSU][OBS-3]
40	
41	namespace gem5
42	{
43	
44	enum class ChaOSLsuTier : uint8_t { F0, F1, F2, F3, F4, F5, F6 };
45	
46	// F6 event sources (09 §2.1 W1 map). TlbHit is FS-only — SE never calls
47	// TLB::lookup (arm/mmu.cc:323-365 translateSe); the enum value exists so the
48	// config surface is uniform, and an SE run selecting it logs zero events.
49	enum class ChaOSLsuEvent : uint8_t { TlbHit, SqForward, DirtyEviction,
50	                                     CasSuccess };
51	
52	// F6 event-source notification hook. The four sources (lsq_unit.cc forward
53	// branch, cache.cc DirtyBit eviction, base.cc SwapReq commit, tlb.cc lookup
54	// hit) each call this when the configured consumer registered a callback.
55	// Inline global in a header-only TU included by exactly one .cc each —
